{# Non-dismissible one-line disclaimer for the footer of generated content pages.

   The top bar (_disclaimer.html.j2) can be dismissed for the browsing session
   since #7421. This line cannot, so a reader who has dismissed the bar still has
   the statement — and a link to the canonical text — somewhere on the page.
   Without it, a dismissed page would carry no disclaimer at all, which is the
   thing design-decisions §11 exists to prevent.

   Wording mirrors the MkDocs `copyright:` footer in mkdocs.yml; keep them in
   step. Styles live in _disclaimer.css.j2 alongside the bar's.

   Included by the templates that have a page footer (disorder, module). The
   other full-page templates have no footer element; see §11 for that gap. #}
<p class="dismech-disclaimer-footer">
    DisMech is an AI-curated research resource and is <strong>not medical advice</strong>.
    <a href="https://dismech.monarchinitiative.org/elements/disclaimer/">Read the full disclaimer</a>.
</p>
